<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The field she stands on, cut from the same picture as the store icon:
     a plum ground with a soft violet glow behind where her head lands.

     The glow is doing real work rather than decorating. Her hair is violet and
     the ground is violet, and at the size a launcher actually draws this — 48dp
     on a crowded home screen — a violet silhouette on a violet field is a
     smudge. Lifting the middle of the field is what keeps her outline.

     Built from flat discs rather than a radial gradient. An inline
     `aapt:attr` gradient is legal here and would be one path instead of six —
     but a launcher icon is the one drawable in the app that no test can check
     on the device that matters, since every variant but release paints its own
     field over this one. Concentric fills approximate the same falloff out of
     primitives with nothing to get wrong.

     The two gold sparkles are the same mark the app puts on anything meant to
     feel special; they sit outside the 66dp safe zone on purpose, so a round
     mask crops them and a squircle keeps them. -->
